<!doctype html>
<!--
  Source of the BuildBox Cheat Sheet, rendered to a one page PDF by
  generate_cheatsheet.sh. @VERSION@ is replaced at generation time.
  Written for people who need to fetch, build and test a project without being
  developers: every card names a task, not a mechanism.
-->
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>BuildBox Cheat Sheet</title>
<style>
  /* Brand palette, same as the documentation site */
  :root {
    --brand: #ee7214;
    --brand-dark: #cc5f10;
    --ink: #1f2430;
    --ink-soft: #5b6472;
    --rule: #e3e6ec;
    --code-bg: #f5f6f8;
    --project: #ee7214;
    --target: #2563eb;
    --build: #16a34a;
    --deliver: #7c3aed;
    --inspect: #0891b2;
    --clean: #dc2626;
    --help: #b45309;
  }

  @page { size: A4 portrait; margin: 0; }

  * { box-sizing: border-box; }

  html, body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    /* Backgrounds and colours must survive printing */
    -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;
    print-color-adjust: exact;
  }

  body {
    width: 210mm;
    height: 297mm;
    padding: 7mm 9mm 5mm;
    font-family: "Helvetica Neue", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 9.1pt;
    line-height: 1.38;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  code, .cmd {
    font-family: "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, "DejaVu Sans Mono", monospace;
  }

  /* --- Header --- */
  header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    justify-content: space-between;
    border-bottom: 2.2pt solid var(--brand);
    padding-bottom: 1.8mm;
    margin-bottom: 2.6mm;
  }
  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 23pt;
    letter-spacing: -0.4pt;
    color: var(--brand);
  }
  h1 span { color: var(--ink); }
  .tagline {
    margin: 0.8mm 0 0;
    font-size: 9.4pt;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .meta {
    text-align: right;
    font-size: 8.2pt;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.45;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .meta strong { color: var(--brand-dark); }

  /* --- Guided path --- */
  .path {
    border: 0.8pt solid var(--rule);
    border-left: 2.6pt solid var(--brand);
    border-radius: 1.6mm;
    padding: 2.6mm 3.4mm 2.8mm;
    margin-bottom: 2.6mm;
    background: #fffdfb;
  }
  .path h2 {
    margin: 0 0 2.4mm;
    font-size: 10.4pt;
    color: var(--brand-dark);
  }
  .path h2 em {
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: normal;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 8.6pt;
  }
  .steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 2.6mm 4mm;
  }
  .step { position: relative; padding-left: 6mm; }
  .step .n {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.1mm;
    width: 4.6mm;
    height: 4.6mm;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--brand);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 7.8pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-align: center;
    line-height: 4.6mm;
  }
  .step .cmd {
    display: block;
    font-size: 9pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: var(--ink);
    word-break: break-word;
  }
  .step .why {
    display: block;
    font-size: 8.2pt;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin-top: 0.4mm;
  }

  /* --- Themed cards --- */
  .cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 2.6mm;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .card {
    border: 0.8pt solid var(--rule);
    border-top: 2.2pt solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 1.6mm;
    padding: 2.6mm 3mm 2.8mm;
    break-inside: avoid;
  }
  .card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 1.8mm;
    font-size: 9.8pt;
    color: var(--accent);
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 1.6mm;
  }
  .card h3 em {
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: normal;
    font-size: 8pt;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .card dl { margin: 0; }
  .card dt {
    font-family: "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, "DejaVu Sans Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 8.6pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--code-bg);
    border-radius: 0.8mm;
    padding: 0.3mm 1mm;
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 1.1mm;
  }
  .card dt:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }
  .card dd {
    margin: 0.4mm 0 0;
    font-size: 8.1pt;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .card dd b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }

  .project { --accent: var(--project); }
  .target  { --accent: var(--target); }
  .build   { --accent: var(--build); }
  .deliver { --accent: var(--deliver); }
  .inspect { --accent: var(--inspect); }
  .clean   { --accent: var(--clean); }

  /* --- Bottom band --- */
  .band {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 1fr;
    gap: 2.6mm;
    margin-top: 2.6mm;
  }
  .band section {
    border: 0.8pt solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 1.6mm;
    padding: 2.6mm 3mm;
  }
  .band h3 {
    margin: 0 0 1.6mm;
    font-size: 9.8pt;
  }
  .words h3 { color: var(--ink); }
  .help {
    border-color: #f0d9ae;
    background: #fffaf0;
  }
  .help h3 { color: var(--help); }
  .words p, .help p {
    margin: 1mm 0 0;
    font-size: 8.1pt;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .words p:first-of-type, .help p:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }
  .words b { color: var(--ink); }
  .help b { color: var(--help); }
  .help code, .words code {
    font-size: 8pt;
    background: var(--code-bg);
    border-radius: 0.7mm;
    padding: 0.2mm 0.8mm;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  footer {
    margin-top: 2mm;
    padding-top: 1.2mm;
    border-top: 0.8pt solid var(--rule);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    font-size: 7.6pt;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header>
  <div>
    <h1>BuildBox <span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p class="tagline">Fetch, build, test and deliver a project. No development experience needed.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="meta">
    version <strong>@VERSION@</strong><br>
    buildbox.trusted-objects.com
  </div>
</header>

<div class="path">
  <h2>A whole session, in six steps <em>&mdash; run each command from inside the project directory</em></h2>
  <div class="steps">
    <div class="step">
      <span class="n">1</span>
      <span class="cmd">bbx clone &lt;url&gt;</span>
      <span class="why">Gets the project and creates its directory.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="step">
      <span class="n">2</span>
      <span class="cmd">cd &lt;project&gt;</span>
      <span class="why">Every command below runs from there.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="step">
      <span class="n">3</span>
      <span class="cmd">bbx target list</span>
      <span class="why">Shows what can be built. Pick a name.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="step">
      <span class="n">4</span>
      <span class="cmd">bbx target set &lt;name&gt;</span>
      <span class="why">Chooses it. It stays chosen.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="step">
      <span class="n">5</span>
      <span class="cmd">bbx target build</span>
      <span class="why">Builds it, fetching whatever is missing.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="step">
      <span class="n">6</span>
      <span class="cmd">bbx target dist</span>
      <span class="why">Produces the deliverable.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="cards">

  <div class="card project">
    <h3>Project <em>get one, know its state</em></h3>
    <dl>
      <dt>bbx clone [-b BRANCH] &lt;url&gt; [dir]</dt>
      <dd>Get an existing project. <b>-b</b> picks a version.</dd>
      <dt>bbx project info</dt>
      <dd>What this project is, and what is already fetched.</dd>
      <dt>bbx project update</dt>
      <dd>Refresh the project <b>settings</b> only. Sources already
          fetched are left as they are.</dd>
      <dt>bbx init [DIR]</dt>
      <dd>Start a new, empty project.</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>

  <div class="card target">
    <h3>Target <em>choose what to build</em></h3>
    <dl>
      <dt>bbx target list</dt>
      <dd>Every target, the current one marked.</dd>
      <dt>bbx target set &lt;NAME&gt;</dt>
      <dd>Work on that target from now on.</dd>
      <dt>bbx target info [NAME]</dt>
      <dd>What it builds, and whether it is fetched.</dd>
      <dt>bbx target pkg [-v] &lt;PKG&gt;</dt>
      <dd>Version and origin of one component. <b>-v</b> tells more.</dd>
      <dt>bbx target tools</dt>
      <dd>The tools this target needs.</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>

  <div class="card build">
    <h3>Build <em>fetch, then compile</em></h3>
    <dl>
      <dt>bbx target clone</dt>
      <dd>Fetch every source the target needs.</dd>
      <dt>bbx target clone -u</dt>
      <dd>Same, and <b>update</b> what is already there.</dd>
      <dt>bbx target build [-v] [-c]</dt>
      <dd><b>-v</b> shows details, <b>-c</b> resumes after a failure.</dd>
      <dt>bbx build &lt;PKG&gt;</dt>
      <dd>One component only. <b>bbx fetch &lt;PKG&gt;</b> just gets it.</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>

  <div class="card deliver">
    <h3>Check &amp; deliver <em>the part you are after</em></h3>
    <dl>
      <dt>bbx target test</dt>
      <dd>Run the target tests. Results in <code>&lt;TARGET&gt;/tests.log</code>.</dd>
      <dt>bbx target dist</dt>
      <dd>Produce the deliverable of the target.</dd>
    </dl>
    <p style="margin:1.6mm 0 0;font-size:8.1pt;color:var(--ink-soft)">
      Deliverables and logs are written in the <code>&lt;TARGET&gt;/</code> directory.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card inspect">
    <h3>Look around <em>where things are</em></h3>
    <dl>
      <dt>bbx shell</dt>
      <dd>A shell inside the build environment.</dd>
      <dt>pg &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; tg &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; pp</dt>
      <dd>Short for <b>project goto</b>, <b>target goto</b> and
          <b>project goto -p</b>: jump to the project, the target,
          the settings.</dd>
      <dt>bbx env</dt>
      <dd>Show the environment a build runs with.</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>

  <div class="card clean">
    <h3>Clean up <em>start over, free space</em></h3>
    <dl>
      <dt>bbx target clean</dt>
      <dd>Remove what was built, keep the sources.</dd>
      <dt>bbx target mrproper</dt>
      <dd>Remove sources and build. Asks first.</dd>
      <dt>bbx stop</dt>
      <dd>Stop this project environment.</dd>
      <dt>bbx instance list</dt>
      <dd>All running environments. <b>instance stop</b> ends idle ones.</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>

</div>

<div class="band">
  <section class="words">
    <h3>Words you will meet</h3>
    <p><b>Project</b> &mdash; a directory holding everything one delivery needs.</p>
    <p><b>Target</b> &mdash; one thing to build: a platform, a variant, a flavour. A project usually has several.</p>
    <p><b>Package</b> &mdash; one component of the build. <b>Tool</b> &mdash; a compiler or utility the build needs.</p>
    <p><b>Profile</b> &mdash; the project settings, in the <code>.bbx/</code> directory.</p>
    <p><b>Container</b> &mdash; the isolated environment builds run in. There is
       one per project, and BuildBox starts it for you.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="help">
    <h3>If something goes wrong</h3>
    <p><b>A build failed.</b> The reason is at the end of <code>&lt;TARGET&gt;/target_build.log</code>.</p>
    <p><b>Sources look outdated.</b> Run <code>bbx target clone -u</code>.</p>
    <p><b>The environment misbehaves.</b> Run <code>bbx stop</code>; the next command restarts it.</p>
    <p><b>"Not in a BuildBox project directory".</b> Move into the project directory first.</p>
  </section>
</div>

<footer>
  <span>BuildBox @VERSION@ &mdash; Trusted Objects</span>
  <span>Full documentation: buildbox.trusted-objects.com</span>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
